assistant_response:
```java
class Parent {
    protected void secure() { System.out.println("Parent"); }
}
class Child extends Parent {
    @Override public void secure() { System.out.println("Child"); }
}
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Parent v = new Child();
        v.secure();
    }
}
```
The child's public implementation is wider than protected, so the complete program compiles and prints Child.
